  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "The 2026 election for Oklahoma's 3rd Congressional District features a Republican primary between 31-year incumbent Frank Lucas and repeat challenger Wade Burleson, while Democrats Suzie Byrd and Jules Roberson compete in their own primary. The district is the largest in Oklahoma, covering 32 counties across the western half of the state, and is rated R+23 by the Cook Political Report, making it one of the most Republican districts in the nation. Lucas, a former chair of both the House Agriculture and Science committees, has not faced a serious general election challenge in decades. The Democratic nominee will face an uphill battle in a district that gave Donald Trump 72% of the vote in 2024.",
